# lahn course: written by the course tools (tools/courses; change it there, and run them again)
version 2
title Ear training
description lahn plays a note, you find it on your bass and play it back: from two notes far apart to every note of a scale, then intervals by name.
instrument bass


level Hear it, find it

chapter High or low
page
  block text
    text lahn plays an open string: the E string or the G string. They're far apart: listen, and play the one you hear.
    text The first drill shows you where it is as it plays: sound and place, together. Then by ear: every string it could be is outlined. Space plays it again.
  block exercise Heard and shown
    id 2
    type notes
    notes E1 G2
    show ear
    where yes
    count 6
    pass 5
    instrument bass
  block exercise By ear
    id 3
    type notes
    notes E1 G2
    show ear
    count 8
    pass 7
    instrument bass
  block exercise No slips
    id 4
    type notes
    notes E1 G2
    show ear
    count 8
    pass 8
    instrument bass

